course: dictionary
lesson: 1381
title: Capitol or capital?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words sound the same but have different spellings and meanings. Capitol, with an o, means a building. Capital, with an a, means a city where a government sits, or money. Context tells you which one is meant.
explain: «On 6 January 2021, while Congress met to confirm the result, a crowd of Donald Trump's supporters broke into the Capitol; people were hurt, and Congress finished confirming Joe Biden's win that night.» Congress meets, and a crowd breaks into a building, so Capitol here means the building where lawmakers meet.
explain: Check by asking: is this a building or a city? Swap your meaning into the sentence. If you read "a crowd broke into the capital", it does not make sense, so you know the word is capitol.
explain: Capital letters are a clue too. «The Capitol» with a capital C names one famous building in Washington, D.C. «Capitol Hill» is the area around it. A state capitol is the building where a state's lawmakers meet.
fact: Capitol (with an o) means a building where lawmakers meet to make laws.
fact: Capital (with an a) means a city where a government sits, or money.
fact: «The Capitol» means the big building with the white dome in Washington, D.C., where the US Congress meets.
fact: «Capitol Hill» is the area in Washington, D.C. where the Capitol stands.
fact: The Capitol is a word used in history too: the Romans had a temple on the Capitoline Hill, but in lessons about the USA it means the building with the dome.
exercise: «On 6 January 2021, while Congress met to confirm the result, a crowd broke into the Capitol.» What is the Capitol? | *A building where lawmakers meet to make laws | A type of bread | A city where the president lives | A tall tower by the sea
exercise: Each US state has its own «state capitol». What does state capitol mean? | The biggest city in a state | A state's oldest school | The money a state keeps in its bank | *The building where a state's lawmakers meet
exercise: Which spelling fits? «The lawmakers met in the ___ building, with its big white dome.» | capital | *capitol
test: Which sentence uses capitol correctly? | *Congress meets in the Capitol, the big building with the white dome. | Each state has a capitol with a big money vault. | The Capitol is a city in the west of England. | The capitol of the USA is Washington, D.C., where the government sits.
test: What is Capitol Hill? | *The area in Washington, D.C. where the Capitol building stands | A hill with a large castle on top | A large shopping centre in London | A hill in a national park
exam: Which word means the building where Congress meets? | castle | congress | *capitol | capital
